Database migrations for the Yagnum API (ADR-014).

Run everything from `app/api`:

    uv run alembic current                          which revision is applied
    uv run alembic upgrade head                     apply what is pending
    uv run alembic revision --autogenerate -m "..." write a new one from models.py
    uv run alembic downgrade -1                     step back one

The connection string is NOT in alembic.ini. `env.py` reads
DATABASE_URL_UNPOOLED from the repo-root `.env` — Neon's *direct* endpoint,
because DDL and a transaction-mode pooler do not mix. The app itself runs on
the pooled DATABASE_URL; see db.py.

After autogenerating, read the generated file before applying it. Alembic
compares metadata to the live database and is good at it, but it cannot know
that a rename was a rename rather than a drop plus an add.
